<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">

IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities 
<br class="ltx_break">for Agentic CLI Systems

</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">IQuest Research
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We present IQuest-Q1, a sparse Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) agentic foundation model with 320B total parameters (15B activated).
IQuest-Q1 is developed through a three-stage process:
(1) <em id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stable and efficient pre-training</em>, combining Stable SplitNorm, Muon, and <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>P with a two-stage curriculum whose second stage increases the coding-data mixture, preserving a wide stability margin between safe and optimal learning rates;
(2) <em id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fine-grained mid-training</em>, expanding the data mixture across domains and formats and progressively extending the context;
and
(3) <em id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-scaffold with multi-version post-training</em>, combining SFT, domain-specialized RL, and MOPD across various scaffolds to integrate complementary training signals and strengthen agentic coding capabilities.
Furthermore, model merging combines different experts and checkpoints from different stages while mitigating conflicts among their parameter updates.
The resulting IQuest-Q1 demonstrates capabilities in both coding and general tasks.
We release IQuest-Q1 as an open-source model to support community research and development.</p>
  
</div>
