<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM-based agents allow language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>, <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>, <a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">80</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">84</a>]</cite> to perform tasks through iterative reasoning, action, and interaction with external environments, rather than merely generating responses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">78</a>]</cite>. Among these environments, command-line interfaces (CLIs) have become one of the most general ways for language models to interact with external systems, use tools, access files, and execute code.
As a result, building more capable agentic models requires stronger CLI capabilities.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we release IQuest-Q1, an open-source agentic foundation model with broad CLI capabilities across a wide range of general and coding tasks, with strengths in software engineering, general-purpose task execution, long-horizon reasoning and execution, and cybersecurity.
We also optimize IQuest-Q1 for real-world CLI use, with reliable tool use and robust performance across different agent harnesses.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Methods.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IQuest-Q1 is trained through a multi-stage pipeline (see <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Results. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 2</span></a>) to progressively develop general knowledge, long-context capabilities, and agentic CLI capabilities.
General pre-training combines Stable SplitNorm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">94</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>, Muon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>P parameterization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">75</a>]</cite> with a two-stage curriculum that increases the coding-data mixture in the second stage. This design improves scaling efficiency while maintaining a wide stability margin between safe and optimal learning rates.
Mid-training then expands the data mixture across domains and formats while progressively extending the context.
Post-training (shown in <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Coding Agent. ‣ 4.1 Large-Scale and Diverse Task Synthesis ‣ 4 Post-Training ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 6</span></a>) builds diverse CLI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> capabilities through synthesized tasks executed in production environments.
Specifically, SFT establishes basic CLI interaction, while RL enhances capabilities through task-level feedback and multi-teacher on-policy distillation (MOPD) consolidates complementary model capabilities from diverse frozen experts into a unified model.
Model merging further combines complementary capabilities from expert models trained for different CLIs, while mitigating conflicts among their parameter updates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 1</span></a> shows the results of IQuest-Q1 on 8 agentic and reasoning benchmarks, highlighting three aspects of its capabilities:
(1) <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Advancing coding capability.</em> IQuest-Q1 demonstrates coding capabilities across benchmarks, including DeepSWE v1.1, CyberGym, and NL2Repo.
(2) <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Broad general agentic and reasoning capability.</em> Beyond coding, IQuest-Q1 demonstrates capabilities on general agentic and reasoning benchmarks, including JobBench, Agents’ Last Exam, and Humanity’s Last Exam.
(3) <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Optimized CLI interaction experience.</em> On our internal IQuest-CLIBench, IQuest-Q1 manifests user-facing CLI interaction capabilities on interactive task.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond benchmark performance, IQuest-Q1 participates in an iterative model-development process built on our internal infrastructure, contributing to the development of its own successors under human supervision.
This human-on-the-loop process provides a practical pathway towards recursive self-improvement, allowing model-generated improvements to accelerate subsequent model iterations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions are summarized as follows:</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IQuest-Q1: an open-weight agentic model optimized for CLI capability.</span>
IQuest-Q1 is a sparse MoE model with 320B total parameters, of which 15B are activated per token, combining substantial general-purpose, coding-agent, and CLI interaction capabilities.
We release its model weights to support further research and development in the community.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLI-centric training pipeline.</span>
We build the training pipeline around CLI-based agentic interaction. Pre-training progressively develops the capabilities required for downstream interaction through staged data mixtures. Post-training specializes these capabilities through task and environment synthesis, multi-scaffold RL, and MOPD to consolidate multiple models into a unified model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model development with human-on-the-loop RSI.</span>
We incorporate IQuest-Q1 into our iterative model-development process, allowing it to evaluate its capabilities and suggest potential improvements through a unified infrastructure interface under human supervision.
This process enables continuous model improvement while shortening the overall development cycle.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30949v1/IQuest-Q1-training-pipeline.svg" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/79;" width="476" height="79"></object>
