<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare IQuest-Q1 with proprietary and open-source models. For proprietary models, we compare against Claude Opus 5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> and GPT-5.6 Sol <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>. For open-source models, we compare with GLM-5.3-Flash <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">89</a>]</cite>, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, Hy3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>, and MiniMax M3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Evaluation Configurations</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each model, we report a publicly available score when one is available; otherwise, we evaluate the model using the corresponding benchmark setup:
(1) <em id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Harness:</em> For agentic coding tasks, we use mini-SWE-agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite> for DeepSWE v1.1, BasicAgent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> for PaperBench, and Claude Code <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> for other tasks. For general agentic tasks, we use our internal harness for search agent tasks and Humanity’s Last Exam, and the benchmark-provided harnesses for other tasks.
(2) <em id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Runtime:</em> We set six-hour limits for CyberGym <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite> and ProgramBench, eight hours for Terminal-Bench 2.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, ten hours for Terminal-Bench 3.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> and 4.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>, and 12 hours for PaperBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 Benchmarks ‣ 5 Evaluation ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a>shows the results under the reported evaluation configurations. We highlight representative results and remaining gaps below.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coding and Software Engineering.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IQuest-Q1 demonstrates a broad range of repository-level coding capabilities, including bug fixing and feature addition, achieving scores of 57.5 on SWE-Bench Pro and 64.6 on DeepSWE v1.1.
It also handles repository generation from natural language across NL2Repo-Bench (63.0) and PaperBench (86.0), covering general programming and research code reproduction.
Terminal-Bench and SkillsBench further evaluate long-horizon terminal workflows and skill-driven coding. On our internal IQuest-CLIBench, IQuest-Q1 further demonstrates practical CLI interaction capabilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General Capabilities.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IQuest-Q1 scores 75.0 on Toolathlon-Verified, 52.7 on AutomationBench, and 77.1 on Claw-Eval, reflecting its capabilities in tool use and multi-step task execution. On BrowseComp and WideSearch, it reaches 85.5 and 81.8, respectively, demonstrating information-seeking capabilities across the two search settings. It also records 55.7 on JobBench and 50.9 on APEX-Agents 1.1, covering task execution in professional workflows. Beyond agentic interaction, scores of 93.3 on GPQA Diamond and 93.0 on IMOAnswerBench-Verified reflect its scientific and mathematical reasoning capabilities. Expert-level reasoning remains challenging: HLE scores of 39.2 without tools and 55.7 with tools indicate room for improvement in both settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Capabilities with CLI Agents</h2>

<figure id="S6.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.30949v1/B7_card_v2.png" id="S6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/271;" width="429" height="271" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S6.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Representative interactive frontend applications generated by IQuest-Q1 from natural-language specifications, covering game worlds, scene editing, and scientific exploration.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Interactive Frontend Generation</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IQuest-Q1 generates diverse interactive frontend applications from user queries, combining visual design, scene construction, and interaction logic in browser-runnable HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. These tasks showcase its CLI coding capabilities by turning implementations into interactive artifacts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We provide examples (see <a href="#S6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 6 Capabilities with CLI Agents ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 7</span></a>) from domains including games, creative tools, and scientific visualization. For example, the underwater sandbox combines an explorable world with building and mining, while the sunset racing game couples vehicle control with camera movement and race-state feedback. The garden editor links flower parameters and planting actions to a 3D scene. Together, they suggest how IQuest-Q1 coordinates rendering, user input, and application state to create interactive web experiences with distinct visual styles.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Iterative Development under Human Supervision</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We illustrate a model development iteration in which an agent built on IQuest-Q1 identifies a capability gap, implements a solution, and evaluates the model under human supervision and intervention.
The iteration targets adaptation to different scaffolds and tool-call schemas. While the model handles familiar schemas well, it can fail on unfamiliar ones, producing 35 tool-call errors in one long-horizon task due to mismatched tool names and parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trace Tool-call Failures and Identify Data Inconsistencies.</span>
The agent traces the failures across 6,054 tool calls and finds that the training data is heavily biased toward a single tool-call schema, with some records containing mismatches between tool definitions and call parameters due to preprocessing. It proposes cleaning these inconsistent records and augmenting the training data with diverse tool-call schemas.
Human experts review the diagnosis and proposed intervention before approving the training run.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implement Mixed-schema Data Augmentation and Model Training.</span>
The agent implements the data cleaning and augmentation pipeline and prepares the experiment configuration. The training run uses 2.35B tokens and 938.7 GPU hours. The resulting model checkpoint is evaluated on held-out schemas and familiar schemas, while checking for performance regressions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This iteration demonstrates the potential of iterative model development with IQuest-Q1, while also highlighting the importance of human supervision.
The agent drives failure analysis, intervention design, implementation, and evaluation, with human experts reviewing key decisions and controlling costly experiments and changes carried forward to subsequent iterations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Cyber Security</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond general software engineering tasks, we further evaluate IQuest-Q1 on defensive cybersecurity tasks, where understanding and validating vulnerabilities are essential for improving software security. IQuest-Q1 achieves a score of 84.5 on CyberGym <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>, a benchmark that evaluates the ability to reproduce and validate real-world vulnerabilities in large open-source codebases, providing evidence to support vulnerability diagnosis and remediation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We further assess the practical utility of these capabilities in real-world security workflows. During a three-day deployment, human cyber security experts, assisted by IQuest-Q1, produced 30 vulnerability reports. All reports were independently validated by fellow security experts, and findings affecting open-source projects were responsibly disclosed to their respective maintainers.
The participating experts reported that IQuest-Q1 provided substantial support for their defensive security work, particularly in understanding and validating security issues.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Limitations</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="Sx1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Text-only input. IQuest-Q1 has no native image, audio, or video input capability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Output reliability. Generated explanations and code may be incorrect. Code changes should be reviewed or verified with task-appropriate tests.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tool integration. Tool calls use the IQuest-specific format in the chat template. Structured tool execution and reasoning extraction require compatible serving parsers and an agent harness.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Challenges in Real-World CLI Tasks. Real-world CLI tasks often require iterative debugging and verification. IQuest-Q1 may overlook constraints, repeat failed attempts, or leave issues unresolved, necessitating human review and supervision.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ongoing development. IQuest-Q1 still has limitations in its capabilities and reliability, and we will continue to advance its capabilities. Furthermore, we release the model weights, deployment configurations, and agent-integration instructions to facilitate further research and continued development in the community.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Conclusion</h2>

<div id="Sx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present IQuest-Q1, an open-source agentic foundation model with broad CLI capabilities. We train IQuest-Q1 through a multi-stage pipeline to progressively develop general knowledge, long-context capabilities, and agentic CLI capabilities. IQuest-Q1 demonstrates capabilities on coding, general agentic tasks, and reasoning-heavy tasks.
Furthermore, IQuest-Q1 participates in our internal iterative model-development loop,
providing a foundation for continuing model development.</p>
</div>
