<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Safe learning rate.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform a grid search over learning rates and classify the resulting training-loss trajectories as stable, warning, or collapsed, as illustrated in <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Safe learning rate. ‣ Appendix A Pre-Training ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 8</span></a>. Stable runs show consistently decreasing loss; warning runs exhibit a transient rebound before recovering, while collapsed runs rebound and remain at high loss. We define the safe learning rate, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathrm{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>safe</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathrm{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as the largest tested learning rate classified as stable.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30949v1/m1_safelr_definition_a025.svg" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/148;" width="333" height="148"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A1.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Representative training-loss trajectories for the model under stable, warning, and collapsed training regimes.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
