<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>P scaling factors.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 𝜇P scaling factors. ‣ Appendix A Pre-Training ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 3</span></a> summarizes the width- and depth-dependent scaling rules used to train IQuest-Q1. Following CompleteP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, we apply an output scaling factor of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> to both the attention and FFN branches. For the attention branch, this factor is incorporated into the output RMSNorm. For the FFN branch, it is applied directly to the branch output.</p>
