<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SWA linear context parallelism with partial halo attention.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ SWA linear context parallelism with partial halo attention. ‣ Appendix A Pre-Training ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 10</span></a> illustrates the setting <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;H&lt;S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;H&lt;S</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of tokens in each contiguous sequence shard and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of preceding tokens accessible to each query. In panel (b), query and key positions are measured relative to the start of the local shard. For a query at position <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, valid key positions satisfy <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-H\leq j\leq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-H\leq j\leq i</annotation></semantics></math>; negative key positions belong to the preceding shard. The horizontal dashed line separates boundary queries from queries whose attention windows lie entirely within the local shard. The pairs <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(O_{\ell},L_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(O_{\ell},L_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(O_{h},L_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(O_{h},L_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the normalized attention outputs and corresponding per-query, per-head log-sum-exp statistics for the local and halo contributions, respectively. Panel (c) depicts execution dependencies schematically.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30949v1/swa_halo_partial_output.svg" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/293;" width="476" height="293"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A1.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overlapping halo exchange with partial attention computation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Recursive Multi-token Prediction.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Recursive Multi-token Prediction. ‣ Appendix A Pre-Training ‣ IQuest-Q1: Advancing Foundation Capabilities for Agentic CLI Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 11</span></a> illustrates the workflow of recursive multi-token prediction. We adopt the MTP architecture of DeepSeek-V3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, which concatenates a hidden representation with a token embedding to form the input to the MTP block. At the first drafting step, the hidden representation comes from the final layer of the backbone model. At each subsequent step, we concatenate the previous step’s output hidden representation with the embedding of the token predicted at that step and feed the result back into the same MTP block, enabling recursive draft generation with shared parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.30949v1/mtp.svg" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/294;" width="476" height="294"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A1.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of recursive multi-token prediction. Here, <math id="A1.F11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the input sequence length and <math id="A1.F11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the drafting step.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
